     ; P3-CLOSURE-RESIDUAL that stops the three instances above, and
     ; carries a TODO(P256-campaign) "pending upstream fix".  Reachable
     ; only from files already retired: the sole [Require Import]s of it
     ; are the three functor instances just excluded, and
     ; [g1_add_func_ok] has zero references anywhere in the tree.  The
     ; two files that read like consumers, RcbGeneralAChain.v and
     ; Group/CurveAdd/CurveAddGeneralA_P256.v, name it only in prose --
     ; neither Requires it.  Excluded so the build stops shipping an
     ; Admitted headline theorem; the Rupicola route
     ; (CurveAddGeneralA*, CurveDoubleGeneralA*, CurveA3_*) already
     ; delivers verified add/double for all three curves.
     Curve.WbwMontgomeryG1GeneralA
     ; The bit-serial scalar-multiplication cluster, superseded by the
     ; wNAF/GLV route.  [BignumShift] provides "shift_scalar" (divide a
     ; bignum by two, hand back the low bit); the other five build a
     ; double-and-add ladder on top of it.  None of the six has EVER
     ; produced a .vo -- BignumShift line 441 ran a [rewrite <- !] whose
     ; RHS occurs inside its own LHS, so it diverged (that, not proof
     ; cost, is the ~4 GB in build_timings), and the other five Require
     ; it.  They were nonetheless in the build, so a whole subtree was
     ; failing per-target while the build reported success elsewhere.
     ; Nothing outside the cluster Requires any of them.
     ; The design moved on deliberately: wNAF_GLV_Func.v, which DOES
     ; build, lists among its changes "Digit loading from word arrays
     ; instead of shift_scalar" -- precomputed wNAF digits allow the
     ; windowed constant-time form, where shifting destroys the scalar
     ; in place and forces a bit-serial ladder.  No Rust or Jasmin
     ; artifact in this tree contains a "shift_scalar"; it never shipped.
     Group.CurveAdd.BignumShift
     Group.CurveAdd.LoopBody
     Group.CurveAdd.ScalarMult
